: <tt>alias NAME</tt>
:: display the definitiion of the alias NAME.
: <tt>alias</tt>
:: display the all definition.

Macros you can use in DEFINITION.

|||mark	|what is this
||$*	|all parameters
||$n	|N-th parameter
||$n*	|parameters after N-th.
||$$	|`$'
||$B	|`|'
||$L	|`<'
||$G	|`>'
||$Q	|'`'
||$@	|Same as $` but convert letters like belows.

! $@'s convert table.

|| from | to
|| / | \
|| -WORD | /WORD
|| WORD/ | WORD\.
|| WORD\ | WORD\.
|| "...""..." | ..."...

for instance

8<
    alias ll "ls -l $*"
>8

! IMPORTANT 

put right values of macro definition into ".." because mark '$'
is the prefix charactor for environment variable when you executed
"option +prefixdollar" or "nyacus -more-unix".

